<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Solar Flare</h1>
<p>Sphere: Fire Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 110)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast solar flare &lt;target&gt;
<a cmd='#'>cast solar flare</a>   (at whoever you are fighting)
use a wand or staff of solar flare
</pre>
<p>The caster raises a palm to the sun, shouts 'yarnolf', and the sun itself 
flares down on the target. It is the strongest of the sun spells, and the 
one that depends most on the hour: it is fearsome at noon, much weaker 
towards dawn and dusk, and terrible against the undead. It needs the sun: 
you must be outdoors, in the daytime (from five in the morning until nine 
at night), under a clear or cloudy sky; rain and storms block it.
</p><p>It does about as well against any armour, and a shield softens it. Casting 
it is an attack and starts a fight. You must be standing. It also turns up 
on wands and staffs among random treasure.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
